WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.373 --> 00:00:01.350
(tense music)

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:02.880
- [Reporter] A flying object crashed

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.400
into the Kremlin in early May.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.040
A few weeks later, several
residential buildings

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.423
were hit in Moscow.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.290
While Russia's strikes
are almost a daily reality

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.680
for the Ukrainian capital Kyiv,

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.040
(bomb explodes)

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.220
these are the first drone
assaults on Russia's capital

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.140
since the war in Ukraine began.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.330
- The population in big cities like Moscow

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:27.420
and St. Petersburg have
been somewhat insulated

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:28.650
from this war.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:31.800
And now, it's basically
come to their doorstep.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:32.760
- [Reporter] The Wall Street Journal

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.640
analyzed social media clips
of the attacks and spoke

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.080
with drone experts to
understand what happened

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:42.093
and what it means for Russia's
involvements in the war.

00:00:43.498 --> 00:00:44.910
(bright music)

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.560
This video on May 3rd

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.690
appears to show one of two drones

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.630
seconds before it was shot
down over the Kremlin,

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:53.940
according to the Russian government.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:57.450
An aviation analyst with defense
intelligence firm, Janes,

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:01.680
said it could have been a small
drone up to 10 feet across,

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.650
most likely launched
from Russian territory.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:07.410
Other aviation experts
the Journal spoke with

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:10.650
suggested the aircraft
had a larger wingspan

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:14.190
with a possible flying range
in the hundreds of miles,

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:15.720
enough to cover the distance

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.990
between Moscow and Ukrainian territory.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:21.750
Several drones could fit that description

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.750
including the Ukrainian UJ-22

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:28.533
and the Chinese-made
Mugin-5 used by both sides.

00:01:29.643 --> 00:01:30.720
(drone explodes)

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.830
On May 30th, a drone crashed
outside the Russian capital

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.630
and several more drones struck

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:39.840
at least three residential
buildings In Moscow.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.870
One verified social media
video captured a drone

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:45.150
with a peculiar airframe design.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.730
Experts say it seemed
to have a push mechanism

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:49.890
with a propeller in the back.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:52.410
This drone is visually
consistent with a type

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:56.340
of kamikaze drone recently
reported on in Ukraine,

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:59.190
according to news agency, Storyful.

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:03.060
Known as Beaver, it is a
self-initiated drone project

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:04.920
by a Ukrainian blogger.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.380
However, some experts note that the shape

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:09.450
of the new drone is slightly different

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:12.123
from the one filmed outside
the Russian capital.

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.870
Military experts say
it's impossible to tell

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:18.450
from the footage who launched the attacks,

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.760
whether it was the Ukrainian military,

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:24.360
or a pro Ukrainian group
working inside Russia.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:27.574
In both cases, Russia blamed Kyiv.

00:02:27.574 --> 00:02:31.741
- (Putin speaks foreign language)

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:35.511
- [Reporter] And Ukraine
denied the allegations.

00:02:35.511 --> 00:02:39.928
- (Mykhailo speaks foreign language)

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:45.390
- One American drone expert
said that use of drones

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:47.550
which can fly hundreds of miles

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:49.950
could also indicate military involvement

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:53.043
in the construction and
development of those drones.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.390
The attacks on Moscow
have raised questions

00:02:57.390 --> 00:03:00.048
about Russia's air defense abilities.

00:03:00.048 --> 00:03:04.215
- (Putin speaks foreign language)

00:03:06.166 --> 00:03:07.380
- [Reporter] Some military experts say

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:10.020
the attacks demonstrate
that Russian airspace

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.240
is not secure and that it's possible

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.553
to evade some of its air defenses.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:18.540
They added that unlike
other more damaging attacks

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.390
that targeted military
bases and oil depots

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:24.660
on Russian territory, the
drone strikes on Moscow

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:27.750
were largely psychological and symbolic.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:30.810
- There'll certainly be an
impact on the Russian psyche

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.880
because very much in these big cities,

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.430
people have felt that they are untouched,

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:37.406
almost, by this war.

00:03:37.406 --> 00:03:40.347
- (Olga speaks foreign language)

00:03:40.347 --> 00:03:43.200
- (Natalya speaks foreign language)

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.447
- The government has used these
attacks, basically to say,

00:03:46.447 --> 00:03:50.700
"See, this is why we are
taking action in Ukraine."

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:54.090
But this has been
somewhat of a wake up call

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:55.260
for the population.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.930
There are recent polls that show

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:01.920
that one of the main topics
that Russians think about today

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:06.720
is the war, that is very
different to, say nine months ago,

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:10.620
when, in the big cities
in particular, in Moscow,

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:13.983
people were very much going
about their daily lives.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.230
- [Reporter] One military expert said

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.750
the Kremlin is trying
to downplay the impacts

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:20.520
of the attacks on the capital.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:22.830
But if they continue,
the question is whether

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:25.650
the Kremlin will manage
to convince the population

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:27.693
to accept this as a new norm.

